[size=5]Smart Slot Filter[/size]

Sets a storage slot's filter from whatever is already sitting in it.

[b]The problem[/b]
Slot filters are how you reserve a slot for one kind of item, and they are what keeps your
employees from stuffing jars into the slot you meant for seeds. Setting one up means opening
the filter panel, scrolling a list, and picking the item. For every slot. In every container.

If the container is already sorted the way you want it, all of that information is right there
in the slots. This mod just reads it.

[b]What it adds[/b]
Two buttons in the slot filter dropdown:

[list]
[*][b]From current item[/b] - sets this slot's filter to whatever is in it
[*][b]Filter all from items[/b] - does that for every non-empty slot in the container, in one click
[/list]

Empty slots are skipped - there is nothing to read a filter from.

That is the whole mod. It writes the same filters you could set by hand, so nothing in your save
depends on it and removing it leaves your filters exactly as they were.

[b]Requirements[/b]
[list]
[*]Schedule I (IL2CPP build)
[*]MelonLoader 0.7.3 or newer
[/list]

[b]Installation[/b]
Drop [b]SmartSlotFilter.dll[/b] into the game's [b]Mods[/b] folder, or install with Vortex.

If you use the MLVScan plugin, add [b]SmartSlotFilter.dll[/b] to [b]WhitelistedMods[/b] under
[b][MLVScan][/b] in [b]UserData/MelonPreferences.cfg[/b], or it will be disabled on startup.

[b]Compatibility[/b]
Built on 0.4.6f5, confirmed working on [b]0.4.6f13[/b]. Multiplayer safe - it only touches your
own UI and sets filters you could set by hand.

The mod hooks the game's filter panel by name. IL2CPP strips method bodies, so those hooks were
found by instrumenting a running game rather than read from source: a rename in a game update
breaks the mod rather than corrupting anything. If it stops working after an update, say so in
the comments.

[b]Also by me[/b]
[url=https://www.nexusmods.com/schedule1/mods/2489]Smart Handlers[/url] - if you are setting up
slot filters, you are the sort of person who wants their employees to stop dumping twenty items
into the first station and ignoring the rest. That one adds limits per slot, portions per trip,
and round robin.

[b]Source and licence[/b]
